.\" Man page for himalaya-mcp-install-ext
.\" Generated: July 2026
.TH HIMALAYA-MCP-INSTALL-EXT 1 "July 2026" "himalaya-mcp 1.8.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
himalaya-mcp\-install-ext \- Install or remove the himalaya-mcp Desktop Extension
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B himalaya-mcp install-ext
[\fIfile\fR]
.br
.B himalaya-mcp remove-ext
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B install-ext
unpacks a
.B .mcpb
package into Claude Desktop's
.B Claude Extensions
directory and registers it in
.BR extensions-installations.json .
If
.I file
is omitted, the command auto-discovers
.B himalaya-mcp-v*.mcpb
in the project root (sorted, newest first).
.PP
The command uses
.B npx --yes @anthropic-ai/mcpb unpack
to perform the unpacking, then writes a default settings file
(\fB{ isEnabled: true, userConfig: {} }\fR) at
.B ~/Library/Application Support/Claude/Claude Extensions Settings/himalaya-mcp.json
on macOS.
.PP
.B remove-ext
deletes the extension directory, the settings file, and the registry
entry. Idempotent.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I file
Path to a
.B .mcpb
package to install. If omitted, the command searches the
project root for
.B himalaya-mcp-v*.mcpb
and picks the newest version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/Claude/Claude Extensions/himalaya-mcp/
(macOS) Unpacked extension directory.
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/Claude/Claude Extensions Settings/himalaya-mcp.json
(macOS) Settings file (created on install).
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/Claude/extensions-installations.json
(macOS) Extension registry; updated on install/remove.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
.I file
not found, no
.B .mcpb
in project root, unpack failed, or unpacked manifest missing.
.SH EXAMPLES
Build and install:
.RS
.nf
npm run build:mcpb
himalaya-mcp install-ext
.fi
.RE
.PP
Install a specific file:
.RS
.nf
himalaya-mcp install-ext ~/Downloads/himalaya-mcp-v1.7.0.mcpb
.fi
.RE
.PP
Remove:
.RS
.nf
himalaya-mcp remove-ext
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR himalaya-mcp (1),
.BR himalaya-mcp-setup (1)
